---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="AI Readiness & Exposure Check"
  description="A 3-minute self-evaluation: 10 questions, an instant reading on AI leverage readiness and AI data exposure. No email needed for the score."
  noindex={true}
>
  <header class="top">
    <div class="wrap">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/">LEADFLOW<span>AUTOMATION</span></a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">A 3-minute self-evaluation · 10 questions</div>
      <h1>How ready is your company for AI — <em>and how exposed is it already?</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Ten questions you (or whoever knows your operations best) can answer without asking IT.
        You get an instant reading on two axes — where AI could create leverage, and where company
        data may already be reaching AI tools without design.
      </p>
      <p class="smallnote">
        This is directional self-reflection, not an audit. Your answers stay in your browser unless
        you choose to request the written readout at the end.
      </p>
      <div class="axes">
        <div class="axis-card"><strong>Axis 1 · AI leverage readiness</strong>Whether your processes, data and ownership are in a shape AI could actually work with.</div>
        <div class="axis-card"><strong>Axis 2 · AI data exposure</strong>How much structure sits between your company's information and the AI tools people already use.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="progress-shell">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="progress-row">
        <div class="bar" aria-hidden="true"><span id="barfill"></span></div>
        <div class="count" id="counter" aria-live="polite">0 of 10 answered</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <form class="quiz" id="quiz" novalidate>
    <div class="wrap">
      <fieldset>
        <legend><span class="qnum">QUESTION 1 · READINESS</span>Is your critical process knowledge written down — or does it live mainly in a few people's heads?</legend>
        <div class="opts">
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q1" id="q1a" value="0" /><label for="q1a">Mainly in people's heads — if two key people left, we'd struggle</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q1" id="q1b" value="1" /><label for="q1b">Partly documented, but often outdated or scattered</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q1" id="q1c" value="2" /><label for="q1c">Documented and maintained for the processes that matter</label></div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset>
        <legend><span class="qnum">QUESTION 2 · READINESS</span>Can the data in your core systems (ERP, CRM, files) be reached by other software — or only by manual export?</legend>
        <div class="opts">
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q2" id="q2a" value="0" /><label for="q2a">Manual export and copy-paste only</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q2" id="q2b" value="1" /><label for="q2b">Some systems have usable connections; others are closed</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q2" id="q2c" value="2" /><label for="q2c">Most core systems can be connected through APIs or integrations</label></div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset>
        <legend><span class="qnum">QUESTION 3 · READINESS</span>Do your key workflows have a clear owner who could approve changing or automating them?</legend>
        <div class="opts">
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q3" id="q3a" value="0" /><label for="q3a">No — ownership is fuzzy; changes stall</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q3" id="q3b" value="1" /><label for="q3b">Some workflows do; many don't</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q3" id="q3c" value="2" /><label for="q3c">Yes — for the important flows, one person could say yes</label></div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset>
        <legend><span class="qnum">QUESTION 4 · READINESS</span>Do you know which three processes consume the most skilled-person hours each week?</legend>
        <div class="opts">
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q4" id="q4a" value="0" /><label for="q4a">No — gut feel only</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q4" id="q4b" value="1" /><label for="q4b">Roughly — we could guess, not size them</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q4" id="q4c" value="2" /><label for="q4c">Yes — we could name them and estimate the hours</label></div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset>
        <legend><span class="qnum">QUESTION 5 · READINESS</span>Has any AI initiative in your company moved past a demo into daily use?</legend>
        <div class="opts">
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q5" id="q5a" value="0" /><label for="q5a">None tried — or demos that impressed and then faded</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q5" id="q5b" value="1" /><label for="q5b">One or two tools in limited, individual use</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q5" id="q5c" value="2" /><label for="q5c">Yes — at least one is part of how a team works daily</label></div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset>
        <legend><span class="qnum">QUESTION 6 · EXPOSURE</span>Do employees use public AI chatbots (ChatGPT and similar) with company information today?</legend>
        <div class="opts">
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q6" id="q6a" value="0" /><label for="q6a">Probably yes — and there's no guidance in place</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q6" id="q6b" value="1" /><label for="q6b">Unsure — we haven't looked into it</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q6" id="q6c" value="2" /><label for="q6c">It's addressed — guidance exists and/or a governed alternative is provided</label></div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset>
        <legend><span class="qnum">QUESTION 7 · EXPOSURE</span>Has anyone defined which company data must never reach an AI tool?</legend>
        <div class="opts">
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q7" id="q7a" value="0" /><label for="q7a">No — it hasn't come up</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q7" id="q7b" value="1" /><label for="q7b">Discussed informally, nothing written</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q7" id="q7c" value="2" /><label for="q7c">Yes — written down and communicated</label></div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset>
        <legend><span class="qnum">QUESTION 8 · EXPOSURE</span>If personal or customer data appeared in an AI prompt, would anyone in the company know?</legend>
        <div class="opts">
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q8" id="q8a" value="0" /><label for="q8a">No — there's no way to know</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q8" id="q8b" value="1" /><label for="q8b">We could probably reconstruct it after the fact</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q8" id="q8c" value="2" /><label for="q8c">We have controls or visibility designed for exactly this</label></div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset>
        <legend><span class="qnum">QUESTION 9 · EXPOSURE</span>Where do the AI tools your company uses process your data?</legend>
        <div class="opts">
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q9" id="q9a" value="0" /><label for="q9a">On the vendors' infrastructure — terms never really reviewed</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q9" id="q9b" value="1" /><label for="q9b">On their infrastructure, but we've reviewed the terms</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q9" id="q9c" value="2" /><label for="q9c">Largely in our own environment, or under agreements we control</label></div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset>
        <legend><span class="qnum">QUESTION 10 · EXPOSURE</span>Has your GDPR / EU AI Act position on AI use been assessed?</legend>
        <div class="opts">
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q10" id="q10a" value="0" /><label for="q10a">Not yet</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q10" id="q10b" value="1" /><label for="q10b">Started — questions raised, not concluded</label></div>
          <div class="opt"><input type="radio" name="q10" id="q10c" value="2" /><label for="q10c">Yes — assessed, with records kept</label></div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="actions">
        <button type="submit" class="btn" id="seeBtn">See my reading</button>
        <p class="hint" id="formHint">Answer all 10 questions to see your result — it appears right here, no email needed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </form>

  <section id="results" aria-live="polite">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="res-head">Your reading</h2>
      <p class="res-sub">
        Two directional signals from your own answers — worth examining, not a verdict on your company.
        The same questions asked of your ops or IT lead may score differently; that difference is itself
        useful information.
      </p>
      <div class="res-grid">
        <div class="res-card">
          <div class="axis">Axis 1 · AI leverage readiness</div>
          <div class="band" id="r-band"></div>
          <div class="score" id="r-score"></div>
          <p id="r-desc"></p>
          <h4>First moves worth considering</h4>
          <ul id="r-moves"></ul>
        </div>
        <div class="res-card">
          <div class="axis">Axis 2 · AI data exposure</div>
          <div class="band" id="e-band"></div>
          <div class="score" id="e-score"></div>
          <p id="e-desc"></p>
          <h4>First moves worth considering</h4>
          <ul id="e-moves"></ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="proofline">
        Built by Gergely Racz — PhD in Engineering (University of Cambridge), 10+ years in AI, 7 patents.
        Architect of production RAG systems in daily use at a multi-billion-dollar US manufacturer.
      </div>

      <div class="next">
        <div class="next-card report">
          <h3>Get your reading + the AI starter pack</h3>
          <p>
            Leave your details and get the <strong>GDPR-AI Checklist</strong> (10 questions before any AI
            tool touches company data) and the <strong>AI Leverage Blueprint</strong> — an executive brief
            on where AI belongs in a company like yours.
          </p>
          <div id="tally-slot"></div>
          <form id="reportForm">
            <div class="fld"><label for="f-name">Name</label><input id="f-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required /></div>
            <div class="fld"><label for="f-email">Work email</label><input id="f-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required /></div>
            <div class="fld"><label for="f-role">Your role</label>
              <select id="f-role" name="role" required>
                <option value="">Select…</option>
                <option>CEO / Founder</option>
                <option>Operations</option>
                <option>IT / Technology</option>
                <option>Other</option>
              </select></div>
            <div class="fld"><label for="f-size">Company size</label>
              <select id="f-size" name="size" required>
                <option value="">Select…</option>
                <option>Under 20 people</option>
                <option>20–100 people</option>
                <option>100–500 people</option>
                <option>500+ people</option>
              </select></div>
            <div class="fld optin">
              <input id="f-optin" name="optin" type="checkbox" />
              <label for="f-optin">Email me occasional practical AI notes (optional)</label>
            </div>
            <button type="submit" class="btn-lite">Send my pack</button>
            <p class="micro">
              Your details are used to deliver the materials above and to follow up on any conversation you
              request — nothing else. Retained per our <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>. Please don't
              submit sensitive operational, personal, regulated or confidential data through this form.
            </p>
          </form>
        </div>
        <div class="next-card map">
          <h3>Or go straight to the real thing</h3>
          <p>
            The self-check points at where to look. The <strong>AI Operating Map</strong> tells you what to
            do: where AI belongs in your company, where it must not go, and the one first move worth funding.
          </p>
          <a class="map-cta" href="https://calendly.com/gergely-estateops/30min" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get your free AI Operating Map →</a>
          <p class="map-note">One 30-minute working session. A written map within 5 business days.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="bottom">
    <div class="wrap">
      Lead Flow Automation · Gergely Racz · <a href="/privacy">Privacy notice</a><br />
      This self-check offers directional self-reflection only. It is not an audit, a compliance assessment, or legal advice.
    </div>
  </footer>
</Base>

<style>
  .wrap { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 20px; }
  .top { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding: 18px 0; }
  .wordmark { font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-size: 15px; color: var(--color-text-primary); text-decoration: none; }
  .wordmark span { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .hero { padding: 56px 0 34px; }
  .eyebrow { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-accent); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  h1 { font-weight: 800; color: var(--color-text-primary); font-size: clamp(30px, 5.5vw, 42px); line-height: 1.12; text-wrap: balance; }
  h1 em { font-style: normal; color: var(--color-accent); }
  .hero p.lead { margin-top: 16px; max-width: 56ch; font-size: 17px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .hero .smallnote { margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); max-width: 60ch; opacity: 0.8; }
  .axes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 12px; margin-top: 24px; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .axes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .axis-card { background: var(--color-bg-elevated); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 16px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .axis-card strong { display: block; color: var(--color-accent); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 5px; }
  .progress-shell { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 5; background: var(--color-bg-deep); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding: 10px 0; }
  .progress-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; }
  .bar { flex: 1; height: 6px; background: var(--color-bg-subtle); border-radius: 999px; overflow: hidden; }
  .bar span { display: block; height: 100%; width: 0; background: var(--color-accent); border-radius: 999px; transition: width 0.25s ease; }
  .count { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .quiz { padding: 26px 0 8px; }
  fieldset { border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--color-bg-elevated); padding: 20px 22px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  legend { font-size: 17.5px; color: var(--color-text-primary); font-weight: 600; padding: 0 6px; line-height: 1.3; }
  .qnum { font-size: 11px; color: var(--color-accent); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.15em; display: block; margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .opts { display: grid; gap: 8px; margin-top: 12px; }
  .opt { position: relative; }
  .opt input { position: absolute; opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; }
  .opt label { display: block; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 7px; padding: 11px 14px; font-size: 14.5px; cursor: pointer; background: var(--color-bg-deep); color: var(--color-text-secondary); transition: border-color 0.15s, background 0.15s; }
  .opt label:hover { border-color: var(--color-accent); }
  .opt input:checked + label { background: var(--color-bg-subtle); border-color: var(--color-accent); color: var(--color-text-primary); }
  .opt input:focus-visible + label { outline: 3px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .actions { padding: 6px 0 30px; text-align: center; }
  .btn { display: inline-block; background: var(--color-accent); color: #06131f; border: none; font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; letter-spacing: 0.04em; padding: 15px 30px; border-radius: 6px; cursor: pointer; }
  .btn:hover { background: var(--color-accent-hover); }
  .btn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--color-text-primary); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .hint { font-size: 13px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-top: 10px; }
  #results { display: none; padding: 8px 0 10px; }
  #results.show { display: block; }
  .res-head { font-size: 26px; color: var(--color-text-primary); font-weight: 700; margin: 26px 0 6px; text-wrap: balance; }
  .res-sub { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); max-width: 62ch; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .res-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .res-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .res-card { background: var(--color-bg-elevated); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-top: 4px solid var(--color-accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px 22px; }
  .res-card .axis { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-weight: 700; }
  .res-card .band { font-size: 28px; color: var(--color-accent); font-weight: 800; margin: 4px 0 2px; }
  .res-card .score { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .res-card p { font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .res-card h4 { font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-accent); margin: 12px 0 6px; }
  .res-card ul { padding-left: 18px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .res-card li { margin-bottom: 5px; }
  .proofline { border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); padding: 10px 16px; background: var(--color-bg-elevated); border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0; font-size: 13px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin: 22px 0; max-width: 66ch; }
  .next { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin: 26px 0 10px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .next { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .next-card { border-radius: 8px; padding: 22px; }
  .next-card.report { background: var(--color-bg-elevated); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .next-card.map { background: var(--color-bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--color-accent); }
  .next-card h3 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--color-text-primary); }
  .next-card p { font-size: 13.5px; margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .fld { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .fld label { display: block; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--color-text-primary); margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .fld input, .fld select { width: 100%; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px 12px; font-size: 14px; background: var(--color-bg-deep); color: var(--color-text-primary); }
  .fld input:focus-visible, .fld select:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset: 1px; }
  .fld.optin { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: flex-start; }
  .fld.optin input { width: auto; margin-top: 3px; }
  .fld.optin label { font-weight: 500; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .micro { font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 10px; opacity: 0.85; }
  .micro a { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .btn-lite { display: inline-block; background: var(--color-accent); color: #06131f; font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; padding: 12px 22px; border-radius: 6px; border: none; cursor: pointer; }
  .btn-lite:hover { background: var(--color-accent-hover); }
  .map-cta { display: inline-block; background: var(--color-accent); color: #06131f; font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; padding: 13px 24px; border-radius: 6px; text-decoration: none; }
  .map-cta:hover { background: var(--color-accent-hover); }
  .map-note { margin-top: 12px; font-size: 12px; }
  .bottom { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); margin-top: 44px; padding: 22px 0 34px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .bottom a { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  #tally-slot iframe { width: 100%; border: 0; min-height: 420px; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { * { transition: none !important; scroll-behavior: auto !important; } }
</style>

<script is:inline>
(function(){
  /* ── Tally wiring ──
     Set TALLY_FORM_ID once the operator's Tally form exists. While empty, the
     native form below stays visible and submits are stored nowhere — the button
     says so honestly. When set, the native form is hidden and the Tally embed
     (with quiz scores as hidden fields) takes its place after the quiz. */
  var TALLY_FORM_ID = '';

  var TOTAL=10;
  var quiz=document.getElementById('quiz');
  var barfill=document.getElementById('barfill');
  var counter=document.getElementById('counter');
  var results=document.getElementById('results');
  var hint=document.getElementById('formHint');

  var BANDS=['Early','Developing','Structured','Architected'];
  function bandIdx(s){ if(s<=3)return 0; if(s<=6)return 1; if(s<=8)return 2; return 3; }

  var R_DESC=[
    'The knowledge and data AI would need are hard to reach — mostly in heads and manual exports. That doesn’t block AI; it means the first wins come from making one process legible before any tool is chosen.',
    'Parts of the company are AI-workable today; others would fight any tool you brought in. The signal worth examining: which single documented, owned process carries the most repeated skilled hours.',
    'Your operations have the shape AI works with: documentation, reachable data, real owners. The question is no longer “can we” but “which constraint first, and with what evidence of payback.”',
    'Rare shape: documented processes, connectable systems, clear ownership, and AI already surviving daily use. The leverage question becomes architectural — what to build on top of what already works.'
  ];
  var R_MOVES=[
    ['Write down ONE critical process end-to-end — the one that would hurt most if its key person left','Ask which 3 processes consume the most skilled hours; even rough numbers change the conversation'],
    ['Pick one documented workflow with a clear owner as the candidate for a first controlled win','Check which core system data is reachable by API before anyone proposes a tool that needs it'],
    ['Size the top 3 skilled-hour processes and rank them by frequency × effort × data availability','Define what evidence would justify a first AI investment — before talking to any vendor'],
    ['Choose the next constraint by commercial value, not by what demos well','Document the acceptance conditions a new capability must meet before it earns production use']
  ];
  var E_DESC=[
    'Company information is likely reaching AI tools without anyone having designed for it — the signals suggest nobody would currently know. Worth examining before it’s examined for you.',
    'Some awareness exists, but little of it is written down or enforced by design. The gap between “we discussed it” and “it’s defined” is where most surprises live.',
    'You’ve done what most companies haven’t: drawn lines and reviewed where data goes. The remaining question is whether the lines are enforced by architecture or by trust.',
    'Data boundaries are defined, visible and largely under your control — the posture that makes AI adoption a design decision instead of a risk decision.'
  ];
  var E_MOVES=[
    ['Ask 5 employees this week — without blame — which AI tools they use and for what','Write a one-page interim guideline: what may and may never go into a public AI tool'],
    ['Turn the informal understanding into one written page, and tell everyone it exists','List every AI tool in use and where each one processes your data — the list is usually longer than expected'],
    ['Test whether your defined boundaries would actually catch a slip, or just discourage one','Extend the review to employee data specifically — it’s the category most often missed'],
    ['Keep the register current as tools change — posture decays quietly','Consider making your boundaries a stated requirement for any new AI vendor']
  ];

  function answered(){
    var n=0;
    for(var i=1;i<=TOTAL;i++){ if(quiz.querySelector('input[name=q'+i+']:checked')) n++; }
    return n;
  }
  function refresh(){
    var n=answered();
    barfill.style.width=(n*10)+'%';
    counter.textContent=n+' of '+TOTAL+' answered';
  }
  quiz.addEventListener('change',refresh);
  refresh();

  function mountTally(r,e,ri,ei){
    if(!TALLY_FORM_ID) return;
    var slot=document.getElementById('tally-slot');
    var native=document.getElementById('reportForm');
    var params=new URLSearchParams({
      alignLeft:'1', hideTitle:'1', transparentBackground:'1', dynamicHeight:'1',
      readiness_score:String(r), exposure_score:String(e),
      readiness_band:BANDS[ri], exposure_band:BANDS[ei],
      source:'summit_qr'
    });
    var iframe=document.createElement('iframe');
    iframe.src='https://tally.so/embed/'+TALLY_FORM_ID+'?'+params.toString();
    iframe.title='Request the starter pack';
    iframe.loading='lazy';
    slot.innerHTML='';
    slot.appendChild(iframe);
    if(native) native.style.display='none';
  }

  quiz.addEventListener('submit',function(ev){
    ev.preventDefault();
    if(answered()<TOTAL){
      hint.textContent='Please answer the remaining '+(TOTAL-answered())+' question(s) — the result appears instantly, no email needed.';
      var first;
      for(var i=1;i<=TOTAL;i++){ if(!quiz.querySelector('input[name=q'+i+']:checked')){ first=quiz.querySelector('input[name=q'+i+']'); break; } }
      if(first){ first.focus(); }
      return;
    }
    var r=0,e=0;
    for(var i=1;i<=5;i++){ r+=parseInt(quiz.querySelector('input[name=q'+i+']:checked').value,10); }
    for(var j=6;j<=10;j++){ e+=parseInt(quiz.querySelector('input[name=q'+j+']:checked').value,10); }
    var ri=bandIdx(r), ei=bandIdx(e);
    document.getElementById('r-band').textContent=BANDS[ri];
    document.getElementById('r-score').textContent='Score '+r+' / 10';
    document.getElementById('r-desc').textContent=R_DESC[ri];
    document.getElementById('e-band').textContent=BANDS[ei];
    document.getElementById('e-score').textContent='Score '+e+' / 10';
    document.getElementById('e-desc').textContent=E_DESC[ei];
    var rm=document.getElementById('r-moves'); rm.innerHTML='';
    R_MOVES[ri].forEach(function(m){ var li=document.createElement('li'); li.textContent=m; rm.appendChild(li); });
    var em=document.getElementById('e-moves'); em.innerHTML='';
    E_MOVES[ei].forEach(function(m){ var li=document.createElement('li'); li.textContent=m; em.appendChild(li); });
    mountTally(r,e,ri,ei);
    results.classList.add('show');
    var reduce=window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    results.scrollIntoView({behavior:reduce?'auto':'smooth'});
  });

  document.getElementById('reportForm').addEventListener('submit',function(ev){
    ev.preventDefault();
    var f=ev.target;
    if(!f.checkValidity()){ f.reportValidity(); return; }
    /* Interim behavior until TALLY_FORM_ID is set — never pretend to send. */
    var btn=f.querySelector('button');
    btn.textContent='Form opens soon — grab the pack at the event booth';
    btn.disabled=true;
  });
})();
</script>
